       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum for ibuprofen in adults is 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for over-the-counter use.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks at this dose:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, cardiovascular events, and fluid retention. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't make this dose safe.\n\nHere are some typical regimens. Which one did you mean?\n- **Mild to moderate pain:** 400 mg PO every 4\u20136 hours as needed, or 600 mg every 6 hours.\n- **Inflammatory conditions or severe pain:** 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day), up to 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum).\n- **A total of 1,600 mg/day:** this might be what was intended, for example 400 mg four times daily.\n\nPlease check the intended dose with your resident or attending, and confirm the indication. Once you tell me the corrected dose and frequency, I'll enter it right away. I can add a note such as \"take with food\" if you want one."
      }
